description:
Give `RootRelativePath::parse` an error type of its own, so the path type no longer depends on the repository layout error and can later move into the domain layer.

## Background

- `RootRelativePath::parse` (`crates/jit/src/repository_state/path.rs:82-104`) returns `RepositoryLayoutError::LexicalEscape` (`path.rs:704`, message "path '{0}' is not lexically confined"), a variant of the layout error that also covers root evidence and symlinked roots. That ties the pure path type to `repository_state`.
- `?` sites whose function returns `RepositoryLayoutError` keep compiling through a `From` conversion: `VirtualPath::worktree`/`data` (`path.rs:360,366`), `RepositoryLayout::new` (`path.rs:504`), `package_tree.rs:200,356`, `initialize.rs:1204` and `gate_run_result_relative_path`'s first parse (`crates/jit/src/repository_state/mutation.rs:510`). Sites under `anyhow` (`commands/snapshot.rs`, `commands/profile.rs:628`) and the two `to_string` mappings (`storage/json.rs:1521`, `storage/artifact_planning.rs:288`) need no change.
- Sites whose function returns another error type rely today on that type's `#[from] RepositoryLayoutError`, and a second conversion step does not chain through `?`:
  - `canonical_path` (`crates/jit/src/storage/redo_record.rs:387`, `RedoRecordError`);
  - `ensure_memory_parent_exists` (`crates/jit/src/storage/repository_state_store.rs:1309`, `RepositoryStateStoreError`);
  - `resolve` (`crates/jit/src/storage/memory.rs:630-656`, parse at `:649`, `RedoApplyError`, whose `Path` variant converts from `RepositoryLayoutError` at `crates/jit/src/storage/redo_apply.rs:84`);
  - `validate_pinned_request` (`crates/jit/src/repository_state/image.rs:916`, `CaptureError`);
  - `create_ancestors` (`crates/jit/src/repository_state/archive.rs:381`, `.map_err(ProducerError::from)`);
  - `tree_path` and `immediate_parent` (`crates/jit/src/repository_state/export.rs:255,266`, `RepositoryExportError`);
  - `gate_run_result_relative_path`'s tail expression (`mutation.rs:514`), which returns the parse result directly.

## Success Criteria

- [hard] REQ-01: `RootRelativePath::parse` returns a dedicated `thiserror` error type that names the rejected text, defined beside the type in `repository_state/path.rs`, with a `From` conversion into `RepositoryLayoutError::LexicalEscape` carrying the same text.
- [hard] REQ-02: Every listed site compiles against the new error type through an explicit conversion into `RepositoryLayoutError` (at `memory.rs:649` a `map_err` keeps the error in `RedoApplyError::Path`), and the rendered message for a rejected path is unchanged.
- [hard] REQ-03: The existing parse tests in `repository_state/path.rs` (`test_path_constructors_and_serde_reject_noncanonical_spellings`, `test_root_relative_path_uses_variant_not_empty_string_sentinel`) pass, and one assertion checks that a rejected parse converts into `LexicalEscape` with the input text.

## Notes

- Behaviour is unchanged: messages and exit classes stay the same.
- Written against the code as it stands after the changes this one follows; line citations name current code.
